      "Step 5 — Split the dose across growth stages. Rarely does all fertilizer go down at sowing. The standard practice for cereals like wheat is: all of the phosphate and potash at sowing (mixed into the seedbed), and nitrogen in splits — typically about one-third at sowing and the rest with the first and later irrigations. Splitting nitrogen matches supply to the plant's demand and reduces losses. Your provincial package of practices gives the exact split for each crop; the principle above is the pattern it follows.",
